anbernic-rg353x-audio-utils (1.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add dedicated full-range Headphones virtual sink.
  * Demote raw ALSA hardware sink so virtual sinks always take priority.
  * Calibrate hardware Master gain staging (reg 215 for SPK, reg 240 for HP).
  * Retune speaker filter to 280 Hz 4th-order Linkwitz-Riley HPF.
  * Preserve separate PipeWire volume levels across jack plug and unplug events.
  * Mute hardware DAC and software sinks during transitions to eliminate bursts and pops.
  * Relax volume limit to allow volume boost up to 150%.
  * Use pw-cli for reliable node ID resolution.

 -- Andrew Rossignol <andrew.rossignol@gmail.com>  Mon, 12 Oct 2026 23:00:00 -0700

anbernic-rg353x-audio-utils (1.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rename package from anbernic-rg353x-headphone-detect to anbernic-rg353x-audio-utils.
  * Add PipeWire and WirePlumber drop-in configurations:
    - Prioritize RK817 internal audio over HDMI.
    - Digital attenuation of -6 dB to prevent RK817 high-pass filter overflow.
    - ALSA buffer headroom tuning.
  * Enhance headphone-jack-detect daemon:
    - Save and restore separate speaker and headphone volume levels across switches.
    - Provide headphone volume safety limiting to protect hearing and reduce noise floor.
  * Update packaging and upgrade migration paths.

 -- Andrew Rossignol <andrew.rossignol@gmail.com>  Mon, 12 Oct 2026 21:00:00 -0700

